{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_rename_manifest", "label": "Rename Manifest (single source of old -> new map)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/contracts/rename-manifest.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single manifest avoids divergent substitutions across README, procedure, fixtures and eight suites, and lets the scope be reviewed before any edit; the implementation consumes it and ContractRuleRenameContractTest.groovy validates the result."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_token_map", "label": "Token Map (folder segment and six file names)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/contracts/rename-manifest.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only the folder segment and the six full file tokens change; short forms (01..03, 01, 02, ...) keep their numeral because the numeral, not the como- prefix, is the ordering criterion."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_reference_inventory", "label": "Reference Inventory (file/line/phase)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/contracts/rename-manifest.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Enumerating each reference by file, line and phase proves that no operational reference is left behind and makes the three-phase split auditable."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_exceptions", "label": "Manifest Exceptions (legacy redirect, negative assertions, out-of-scope dirs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/contracts/rename-manifest.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Negative assertions must contain the old names to prove absence, and the legacy redirect must keep the old path for compatibility; without an explicit exception list a zero-old-name sweep would either fail forever or mask real leftovers."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_rulephase_detection", "label": "rulePhase Detection Table (p1LegacyOld, p1Current, p1New)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/contracts/rename-manifest.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FileRenameContractTest must stay green in every intermediate phase, so the suite derives rulePhase from the existence of the new folder and new names instead of hardcoding one final expected state."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_contract_rulerename_contract_test", "label": "ContractRuleRenameContractTest.groovy (phase-aware contract suite)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/contracts/rename-manifest.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A dedicated suite is preferred over extending PathRenameContractTest (which covers the feature 006 root rename) so the new responsibility is clear and the spec criteria fail the build instead of relying on manual review."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_rename_manifest", "target": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_contracts_rename_manifest_token_map", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/contracts/rename-manifest.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_011_rename_contract